     1,
     "Hi Cindy,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m pretty sure I won&#39;t change this since single quotes and double quotes in R are interchangeable. And I don&#39;t recommend copying and pasting from a PDF document, as you&#39;ve found out PDF readers do weird things surrounding copy/paste. Rather, use the internal documentation from within R. You should have no problems copying and pasting either the HTML or internal formats.</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Jeff<br><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Aug 5, 2012 at 1:14 PM, CB <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cindyb...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><font>Hi all,</font></div><div><font><br></font></div><div><font>Thanks Jeff for this fantastic package and the complete documentation.<br>\r\n</font></div><div><font><br></font></div><div><font>I found a small error regarding the use of single quotes in the documentation, <a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/Rook/Rook.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/Rook/Rook.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793245055629000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10rxycxolQqCc5NInGMPnR\">http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/Rook/Rook.pdf</a></font></div>\r\n<div><font><br></font></div><div><font>It uses single quotes, <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,242,204)\">  &#39;  </span> ,  for character strings and variable names. However, they get rendered in the pdf as <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,242,204)\">curly left-handed or smart quotes</span>. R interprets these are &quot;<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,242,204)\">commas</span>&quot;. So when I copy/paste the example code from the pdf into R, I get errors. For example:</font></div>\r\n<div><font><br></font></div><div><font><br></font></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><span style=\"font-size:large;background-color:rgb(217,234,211)\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:large;background-color:rgb(217,234,211)\">copied from the pdf:</span></div>\r\n</blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><a href=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-w_aRPTI3Up8/UB60vMit1WI/AAAAAAAAAB4/n7P3TwywQyI/s1600/curlyexample.tiff\" style=\"text-align:center;margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-w_aRPTI3Up8/UB60vMit1WI/AAAAAAAAAB4/n7P3TwywQyI/s1600/curlyexample.tiff&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793245055629000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2aBRQWr9AHjUDef-wt8Nai\"><img border=\"0\"></a></div>\r\n</blockquote><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(217,234,211)\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(217,234,211)\">pasted into the R</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(217,234,211)\"> console, and hit enter</span></font></div>\r\n</blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3ZGiKjxRqnE/UB6vhmbCOkI/AAAAAAAAABo/wdzQ9_ZXIeA/s1600/curlyexampleR.tiff\" style=\"text-align:center;margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3ZGiKjxRqnE/UB6vhmbCOkI/AAAAAAAAABo/wdzQ9_ZXIeA/s1600/curlyexampleR.tiff&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793245055629000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2rBCwXTHsZqPpX-1lW-QL_\"><img border=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"76\"></a></font></div>\r\n</blockquote><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font size=\"4\" style=\"background-color:rgb(217,234,211)\">comma, easily missed by newbies, is R&#39;s interpretation of the code, and the explanation of the error:</font></div>\r\n</blockquote><div><font size=\"4\"><br></font></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><p><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"4\">Error: unexpected input in &quot;system.file(<span style=\"background-color:rgb(234,153,153)\">‚</span>&quot;</font></p>\r\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><font size=\"4\" style=\"background-color:rgb(217,234,211)\">code typed by hand and hit enter, gives correct result:</font></blockquote>\r\n<div> <br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><a href=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-VzQ8lezKziM/UB624KKt8VI/AAAAAAAAACA/uVN1Owo7dH4/s1600/curlyexampleRgood.tiff\" style=\"text-align:center;margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-VzQ8lezKziM/UB624KKt8VI/AAAAAAAAACA/uVN1Owo7dH4/s1600/curlyexampleRgood.tiff&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793245055629000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1YrAQKFujEc4uZKWTIFxP1\"><font size=\"6\"><img border=\"0\"></font></a></blockquote>\r\n <br><div>\r\n<p><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><font>I know this is a small thing to experienced programmers, and not a problem if you type the code by hand, but it caused me hours of frustration as I was trying to learn Rook by copy/pasting large blocks of code, ie, on pages 13-14.</font></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><font>To fix it in your next version of the docs,it probably has something to do with the word processing settings: perhaps use &quot;dumb&quot; instead of &quot;smart&quot; quotes.</font></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><font>I think Rook is fantastic. Hope this helps,</font></span></p><p><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><font>CB</font></span></p></div></blockquote></div><br></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
